        {
          "id": 1865320331,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "I do remember that SIP over TCP seemed to be hardly used (apart from testing that stacks could use it if the PDU size became large enough).\n\nBut will a SIP stack really retransmit over TCP?  Surely the TCP stack handles any necessary retransmissions (and it would only be passed to the SIP stack once) ?",
          "author": {
            "id": 6810036,
            "username": "martin.r.mathieson",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Martin Mathieson",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/030414c33f619ee28811cd9c073802ef2267d160ab2744eb8427bd49af4c7998?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/martin.r.mathieson"
          },
          "created_at": "2024-04-16T14:24:41.933Z",
          "updated_at": "2024-04-17T05:22:18.297Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 295789178,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": true,
          "resolved_by": {
            "id": 6792385,
            "username": "AndersBroman",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "AndersBroman",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/132fb48f26018ea9516aea909144af3c3a94eaf2ba477efaa9a232abe80d322c?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/AndersBroman"
          },
          "resolved_at": "2024-04-17T05:22:18.297Z",
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 15259,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 1865421581,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "It probably does not, however the function that checks retransmission is also the one that adds it to the hash table to pair requests and replies, and that is useful. I suppose it could be altered to add it to the table but not try to check for retransmission.\n\n> Surely the TCP stack handles any necessary retransmissions (and it would only be passed to the SIP stack once) ?\n\nIf the user happens to disable the \"Analyze TCP sequence numbers\" then the TCP stack doesn't handle it.. but then anything that is segmented ends up being Continuation Data I think.\n\nE.g., see #19753, where this does make request and reply pairing work. Also that one features out of order TCP, so that preference has to be on for it to work.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2024-04-16T15:10:33.645Z",
          "updated_at": "2024-04-17T05:22:18.297Z",
